'--view=[How live per-unit output renders while a task runs\: \`auto\` (default), \`tiles\`, \`panes\`, or \`stream\`. Applies only when running tasks (\`toven run\` / \`toven <task>\`); overrides the \`\[toven\].view\` setting. Redirected, piped, \`--output jsonl\`, and non-interactive runs always use the linear \`stream\` shape regardless of this flag]:MODE:((auto\:"Pick the richest shape the environment supports (default)"
tiles\:"One live, content-sized tile per in-flight unit in a single terminal"
panes\:"One multiplexer pane per unit (opt-in; requires a supported multiplexer)"
stream\:"A single linear stream, log-friendly (each unit flushed as one block)"))' \
'--timeout=[When running tasks only\: bound how long any single execution unit may run before it is cooperatively cancelled and reported as a timeout failure (duration string, e.g. \`30s\`, \`5m\`)]:DURATION:_default' \
'-j+[When running tasks only\: cap how many units run concurrently, overriding the \`\[toven\].max_parallel\` setting. \`--jobs 1\` forces strictly serial execution (one unit at a time), which streams each unit'\''s output inline as a single continuous log instead of buffered per-unit blocks]:N:_default' \
'--jobs=[When running tasks only\: cap how many units run concurrently, overriding the \`\[toven\].max_parallel\` setting. \`--jobs 1\` forces strictly serial execution (one unit at a time), which streams each unit'\''s output inline as a single continuous log instead of buffered per-unit blocks]:N:_default' \
'--compute-budget=[When running tasks only\: cap the CPU parallelism handed to each spawned tool, overriding \`\[toven\].compute_budget\`. The engine splits this total budget across the units running concurrently and injects each share as an ecosystem env var (e.g. \`GOMAXPROCS\`). \`auto\` sizes it to the host CPUs; \`inherit\` (or \`0\`) injects nothing]:BUDGET:_default' \
'--base=[Change-selection commands only\: override the diff baseline reference (per-member under a federation; falls back to \`\[\[members\]\].base_ref\` / \`\[project\].base_ref\`)]:REF:_default' \
'*--module=[Execution/affected/explain verbs and bare tasks\: activate modules by selector — a bare name (\`core\`), \`ecosystem\:name\` (\`rust\:core\`), \`workspace/name\` (\`backend/api\`), or a glob (\`rust\:*\`, \`rskit-*\`) — bypassing changed-selection (repeatable)]:SELECTOR:_default' \
'*--workspace=[Execution/affected/explain verbs and bare tasks\: activate every module owned by a workspace, by id or glob (\`backend\`, \`rust\:contrib\`, \`backend*\`), bypassing changed-selection (repeatable)]:SELECTOR:_default' \
'--watch-debounce-ms=[Watch only\: trailing-edge debounce window, in milliseconds, for coalescing a burst of filesystem events into one rerun (default 200)]:MS:_default' \
'*--patch=[Release tag/publish only\: force \`<module>\` to bump at the patch level (repeatable). Given with no value, bumps every in-scope module at patch (lock-step / ecosystem-wide). Highest precedence with the other level flags and \`--set-version\`; a module named in two level flags or a level flag plus \`--set-version\` is a usage error]::MODULE:_default' \
'*--minor=[Release tag/publish only\: force \`<module>\` to bump at the minor level (repeatable). Given with no value, bumps every in-scope module at minor (lock-step / ecosystem-wide)]::MODULE:_default' \
'*--major=[Release tag/publish only\: force \`<module>\` to bump at the major level (repeatable). Given with no value, bumps every in-scope module at major (lock-step / ecosystem-wide)]::MODULE:_default' \
'*--set-version=[Release tag/publish only\: pin \`<module>=<x.y.z>\` to an explicit target version (repeatable), or a bare \`<x.y.z>\` to set every in-scope module to that version (lock-step / ecosystem-wide, root included)]:[MODULE=]VERSION:_default' \
'--pre=[Release tag/publish only\: cut a prerelease on a configured channel (\`rc\`/\`alpha\`/\`beta\`)]:CHANNEL:_default' \
'--out-dir=[Release sbom/depgraphs only\: directory to write generated artifacts into (created if absent; defaults to \`target/toven/release\`)]:PATH:_files' \
'--target=[Release package only\: the target triple to package (e.g. \`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\`); selects the declared archive asset and the built binary under \`target/<triple>/release/\`]:TRIPLE:_default' \
'--binary=[Release package only\: explicit path to the already-built binary to archive; defaults to \`target/<triple>/release/<binary>\`]:PATH:_files' \
'--line=[Coverage only\: override the absolute line-coverage floor for this run (percentage, \`0..=100\`); wins over the \`\[…coverage\].line\` config default]:PCT:_default' \
'--function=[Coverage only\: override the function-coverage floor for this run (percentage; gated only where the ecosystem measures functions)]:PCT:_default' \
'--region=[Coverage only\: override the region-coverage floor for this run (percentage; gated only where the ecosystem measures regions)]:PCT:_default' \
'--changed-line=[Coverage only\: override the changed-lines floor for this run (percentage; applied to changed files under a changed selection)]:PCT:_default' \
'--enforcement=[Coverage only\: override how a below-threshold verdict is enforced (\`block\` fails the gate; \`advisory\` reports without failing)]:MODE:((block\:"Fail the gate closed on a below-threshold dimension"
advisory\:"Measure and report the shortfall without failing"))' \
'--force=[Init only\: regenerate one \`\[ecosystems.<id>\]\` section]:ID:_default' \
'--root=[Init only\: project root to onboard against]:PATH:_files' \
'--format=[Graph only\: dependency-graph rendering format]:FORMAT:((text\:"Indented adjacency text"
dot\:"Graphviz DOT"))' \
'--dry-run[Preview what would run, without executing anything]' \
'--explain[Preview what would run, with the reasoning for each unit]' \
'--fail-fast[Stop scheduling after the first failure (when running tasks only)]' \
'--no-cache[Execution verbs only\: bypass the task cache (every unit re-runs; records are neither read nor written)]' \
'--refresh[Execution verbs only\: ignore cached results and re-run every unit, but still write the fresh results back (distinct from \`--no-cache\`, which neither reads nor writes). Mutually exclusive with \`--no-cache\`]' \
'--merge-base[Change-selection commands only\: diff against \`merge-base(reference, HEAD)\`]' \
'--dependents[Execution/affected/explain verbs and bare tasks\: with \`--module\`/ \`--workspace\`, also activate the reverse-dependents closure (everything that depends on the selection)]' \
'--dependencies[Execution/affected/explain verbs and bare tasks\: with \`--module\`/ \`--workspace\`, also activate the forward-dependencies closure (everything the selection needs)]' \
'--watch[When running tasks only\: keep running, re-executing the affected subgraph each time a watched source file changes (Ctrl+C exits)]' \
'*-v[Increase reporter verbosity (repeatable; execution verbs only)]' \
'*--verbose[Increase reporter verbosity (repeatable; execution verbs only)]' \
'*-q[Decrease reporter verbosity (repeatable; execution verbs only)]' \
'*--quiet[Decrease reporter verbosity (repeatable; execution verbs only)]' \
'--no-push[Release only\: skip pushing the release commit and tags]' \
'--offline[Release tag/publish only\: skip registry \`published_versions\` lookups and anchor idempotency on the release tag only]' \
'--download[Release verify only\: download the declared assets from the hosted release and verify signature + checksum before extraction, instead of verifying the local \`dist/\` archives]' \
'--no-run[Release verify only\: skip executing the packaged binary; presence, signature, and checksum are still enforced]' \
'--non-interactive[Init only\: answer the wizard non-interactively, accepting every default]' \
'--yes[Release tag/publish only\: confirm the real mutation. Kept separate from \`--non-interactive\` so authorizing a release is always a deliberate flag, never something learned as harmless on \`init\`]' \
'--print[Init only\: render the \`toven.toml\` to stdout and write nothing]' \
'--auto-install[Driver/federation only\: provision missing drivers automatically]' \
'-h[Print help (see more with '\''--help'\'')]' \
'--help[Print help (see more with '\''--help'\'')]' \
':task -- Task whose blast radius is projected:_default' \
&& ret=0
